Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:39:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): CLI schedule/block from outside refuses a card a
 live worker owns; pin live_claim own-holder and primary gates [daveey]

PR #1517 fenced the agent tools kanban_schedule/kanban_block, but the sibling
CLI path (hermes kanban schedule|block <id>, used over ssh) still passed
expected_run_id=None for an outside caller and ended the live worker's open run
underneath it (repro on aabc3f0c2d). _guarded_park now asks the same
tools.kanban_tools_live_park.live_claim() per id when the caller does not own
the run, and refuses that id with the tool's text (holder, run, Nothing changed,
steer with hermes kanban comment, stop with reclaim/archive). Bulk --ids refuses
only the live ids, parks the rest and exits 1. kb.schedule_task/block_task are
unchanged, so internal parkers keep their behaviour.

Tests: CLI schedule, block, bulk (live + ready), own-run CLI park, dead-worker
claim, ready card, the Board-claim incident shape via the CLI; plus pins for two
live_claim() guards no test exercised (holder == own; non-primary board).

Card: t_01a1d0622df6ea87
